	(descr "Extracted verbatim (pads, graphics, 3D model reference) from the footprint embedded as U1 in the original hand-drawn FoveaCamDuo-PCB.kicad_pcb (KiCad 9, git 289fb6c); not in the stock KiCad 10 library. Original library id: Module:Teensy_4_0. V0.1, owner decision 2026-10-07 (\"Oval is ok if it prevents necks like this\"): every pad an oval (pad G a rounded rectangle of the same size) 2.0 mm along the pin axis, centred on the unchanged 1.0 mm drill. Width across the pin row 1.36 mm (owner decision 2026-10-07, fab review option (b), docs/reviews/fab-process-review.md F4: plated ring 0.18 mm across the row = JLCPCB 2-layer 1 oz minimum; was 1.27 mm / 0.135 mm in v0.1.0), so a full-width 0.254 mm track between two pads keeps 0.463 mm to each (THT pad clearance 0.4 mm, lib/rules.py, relaxed by the owner the same day). Ring 0.5 mm along the pin (original 0.389 mm). Original pads: 1.778 mm round (G: 1.778 mm rounded square).")
